  "content": {
    "title": "TCU basketball beats Ohio State on Xavier Edmonds shot in March Madness",
    "text": "Updated March 19, 2026, 5:28 p.m. ETTCU basketball beat Ohio State, 66-64, in a classic start to March Madness in Greenville, South Carolina.Xavier Edmonds made a shot in the paint while double-teamed with 4.1 seconds left and No. 9 seed TCU beat No. 8 Ohio State, 66-64, in a first-round Men's NCAA Tournament game at Bon Secours Wellness Arena on March 19.TCU had a 15-point lead at the half but trailed in the final two minutes. The Horned Frogs (23-11) advanced to play No. 1 seed Duke on March 21 for the right to go to the Sweet 16 of the East Regional in Washington D.C.March Madness tickets for Greenville Regional in NCAA TournamentTCU had three players who combined for 50 points. Edmonds had 16 points and eight rebounds, David Punch had 16 points and 13 rebounds, and Micah Robinson had 18 points on 4-for-6 on 3-pointers.TCU is making its fifth appearance in the NCAA Tournament in the past eight years that a tournament was held. It was cancelled in 2020 because of COVID. The Horned Frogs' best finish was making it to the Elite Eight in 1968.Ohio State has not been the NCAA Tournament since 2022, when it was a No. 7 seed and beat Loyola Chicago before falling to No. 2 seed Villanova.TCU basketball vs Ohio State in March Madness live score updates 26.2 in second half: TCU 64, Ohio State 64This is the way March Madness should start. Down to the wire. Micah Robinson with a 3-pointer for a 64-61 lead, then Bruce Thornton with an answer 3-pointer. 7:05 in second half: Ohio State 51, TCU 50Ohio State is on an 11-1 run, and it's been 27-11 in the second half. Bruce Thornton still has only five points, so he's helping in other ways. 8:40 in second half: TCU 49, Ohio StateHere come the Buckeyes. It's a 7-0 run and TCU needs a timeout. OSU crowd coming to life as well. 14:10 in second half: TCU 43, Ohio State 33Jayden Pierre is putting on a master class of defense against Ohio State star Bruce Thornton, who has five points on only five shots. He hasn't scored since 12:21 of the first half. He hit a 3-pointer for OSU's first basket of the game and has made one field goal since. Halftime: TCU 29, Ohio State 24The Horned Frogs made 6 of 9 shots from 3-point territory to finish the half. Micah Robinson has 13 points and Xavier Edmonds has 10. They are a combined 5-for-5 from three. Ohio State seems to be reeling, and TCU seems to have the crowd on its side. 2:28 in first half: TCU 31, Ohio State 24TCU has made four of its last seven 3-pointers after a 1-for-4 start. Ohio State is 2-for-9 from long range. Micah Robinson has 10 points for the Frogs. 6:08 first half: TCU 23, Ohio State 18Xavier Edmonds made back-to-back 3-pointers for TCU, following a 3-pointer by Micah Robinson, to give the Horned Frogs a 23-15 lead. They started just 6-for-19 shooting and missed three easy ones on one possession. But those threes have given TCU a lift. 15:22 first half: TCU off to strong startBrock Harding scored five points early and TCU has an 8-5 lead against Ohio State. Jayden Pierre has the defensive assignment so far on Buckeyes star Bruce Thornton, who hit a three pointer early. TCU might have edge in bench play against OSU TCU coach Jamie Dixon believes the Horned Frogs could have more success with backups in the game against Ohio State. “One of our strengths is our bench,” Dixon said. “When I say bench, the two guys coming off are really starters. We start seven guys. If you look at our minutes, it’s pretty even between those seven. ... I don’t know if I've ever just played seven guys like this, but this has worked out well for our guys.” What time do TCU, Ohio State play in Greenville in 2026 NCAA tournament?Date: March 19, 2026Time: 12:15 p.m. ETLocation: Bon Secours Wellness Arena; Greenville, South CarolinaAnnouncers: Ian Eagle, Bill Raftery, Grant Hill and Tracy WolfsonWhat channel is TCU vs. Ohio State in March Madness first roundNo. 8 Ohio State will play No. 9 seed TCU on March 19 (12:15 p.m.) at Bon Secours Wellness Arena in Greenville in the East Region of the NCAA Tournament. TV channel: CBSStreaming: Stream on Sling TVTodd Shanesy covers high school athletics for the Greenville News, Spartanburg Herald-Journal and Anderson Independent Mail in the USA TODAY Network. Contact him by email at todd.shanesy@shj.com. Follow him on X, formerly called Twitter, at @ToddShanesySHJ.",
